\s1 Laws against Eating Blood
\p \v 10 \w If anyone|strong="H376"\w* \w from|strong="H4480"\w* \w the house|strong="H1004"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w* \w or a foreigner|strong="H1616"\w* \w living|strong="H1481"\w* \w among them|strong="H8432"\w* \w eats|strong="H398"\w* \w any|strong="H3605"\w* \w blood|strong="H1818"\w*, \w I will set|strong="H5414"\w* \w My face|strong="H6440"\w* \w against that person|strong="H5315"\w* \w and cut him off|strong="H3772"\w* \w from among|strong="H7130"\w* \w his people|strong="H5971"\w*. \v 11 \w For|strong="H3588"\w* \w the life|strong="H5315"\w*\f + \fr 17:11 \ft Literally \fqa the soul\ft ; also in verse 14\f* \w of the flesh|strong="H1320"\w* \w is in the blood|strong="H1818"\w*, \w and I|strong="H589"\w* \w have given|strong="H5414"\w* \w it|strong="H1931"\w* to you \w to make atonement|strong="H3722"\w* \w for|strong="H5921"\w* \w your souls|strong="H5315"\w* \w upon|strong="H5921"\w* \w the altar|strong="H4196"\w*; \w for|strong="H3588"\w* \w it is|strong="H1931"\w* \w the blood|strong="H1818"\w* \w that makes atonement|strong="H3722"\w* \w for the soul|strong="H5315"\w*. \v 12 \w Therefore|strong="H5921"\w* \w I say|strong="H559"\w* \w to the Israelites|strong="H1121"\w*, ‘\w None|strong="H3605"\w* of you \w may eat|strong="H398"\w* \w blood|strong="H1818"\w*, \w nor may|strong="H3808"\w* \w any foreigner|strong="H1616"\w* \w living|strong="H1481"\w* \w among you|strong="H8432"\w* \w eat|strong="H398"\w* \w blood|strong="H1818"\w*.’
\p \v 13 \w And if any|strong="H376"\w* \w Israelite|strong="H1121"\w* \w or foreigner|strong="H1616"\w* \w living|strong="H1481"\w* \w among them|strong="H8432"\w* \w hunts down|strong="H6679"\w* \w a wild|strong="H2416"\w* \w animal|strong="H6718"\w* \w or|strong="H176"\w* \w bird|strong="H5775"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w may be eaten|strong="H398"\w*, \w he must drain|strong="H8210"\w* \w its blood|strong="H1818"\w* \w and cover|strong="H3680"\w* \w it with dirt|strong="H6083"\w*. \v 14 \w For|strong="H3588"\w* \w the life|strong="H5315"\w* \w of all|strong="H3605"\w* \w flesh|strong="H1320"\w* \w is its blood|strong="H1818"\w*. \w Therefore I have told|strong="H559"\w* \w the Israelites|strong="H1121"\w*, ‘\w You must not|strong="H3808"\w* \w eat|strong="H398"\w* \w the blood|strong="H1818"\w* \w of any|strong="H3605"\w* \w living thing|strong="H1320"\w*, \w because|strong="H3588"\w* \w the life|strong="H5315"\w* \w of all|strong="H3605"\w* \w flesh|strong="H1320"\w* \w is its blood|strong="H1818"\w*; \w whoever|strong="H1931"\w* \w eats it|strong="H398"\w* \w must be cut off|strong="H3772"\w*.’
\p \v 15 \w And any|strong="H3605"\w* \w person|strong="H5315"\w*, \w whether native|strong="H249"\w* \w or foreigner|strong="H1616"\w*, \w who|strong="H834"\w* \w eats|strong="H398"\w* \w anything found dead|strong="H5038"\w* \w or mauled by wild beasts|strong="H2966"\w* \w must wash|strong="H3526"\w* \w his clothes|strong="H899"\w* \w and bathe|strong="H7364"\w* \w with water|strong="H4325"\w*, \w and he will be unclean|strong="H2930"\w* \w until|strong="H5704"\w* \w evening|strong="H6153"\w*; \w then he will be clean|strong="H2891"\w*. \v 16 \w But if|strong="H518"\w* \w he does not|strong="H3808"\w* \w wash|strong="H3526"\w* \w his clothes and bathe|strong="H7364"\w* \w himself|strong="H1320"\w*, \w then he shall bear|strong="H5375"\w* \w his iniquity|strong="H5771"\w*.”
\c 18
\s1 Unlawful Sexual Relations
\r (\ref Matthew 5:27–30|MAT 5:27-30\ref*)
\p \v 1 \w Then the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w said|strong="H1696"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Moses|strong="H4872"\w*, \v 2 “\w Speak|strong="H1696"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w the Israelites|strong="H1121"\w* \w and tell|strong="H559"\w* \w them|strong="H413"\w*: \w I|strong="H589"\w* \w am the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w your God|strong="H430"\w*. \v 3 \w You must not follow|strong="H6213"\w* \w the practices|strong="H4639"\w* \w of the land|strong="H776"\w* \w of Egypt|strong="H4714"\w*, \w where|strong="H834"\w* \w you used to live|strong="H3427"\w*, \w and you must not follow the practices|strong="H4639"\w* \w of the land|strong="H776"\w* \w of Canaan|strong="H3667"\w*, \w into which|strong="H834"\w* \w I|strong="H589"\w* \w am bringing you|strong="H935"\w*. \w You must|strong="H6213"\w* \w not|strong="H3808"\w* \w walk|strong="H1980"\w* \w in their customs|strong="H2708"\w*.
\p \v 4 \w You are to practice|strong="H6213"\w* \w My judgments|strong="H4941"\w* \w and keep|strong="H8104"\w* \w My statutes|strong="H2708"\w* \w by walking|strong="H1980"\w* in them. \w I|strong="H589"\w* \w am the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w your God|strong="H430"\w*. \v 5 \w Keep|strong="H8104"\w* \w My statutes|strong="H2708"\w* \w and|strong="H853"\w* \w My judgments|strong="H4941"\w*, \w for|strong="H834"\w* \w the man|strong="H120"\w* \w who does these things|strong="H6213"\w* \w will live|strong="H2421"\w* by them.\f + \fr 18:5 \ft Cited in \ref Romans 10:5|ROM 10:5\ref* and Galatians 3:12; see also Ezekiel 20:11, 13, and 21.\f* \w I|strong="H589"\w* \w am the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*.
\p \v 6 \w None of|strong="H376"\w* \w you are to approach|strong="H7126"\w* \w any|strong="H3605"\w* \w close relative|strong="H7607"\w* \w to have sexual relations|strong="H1540"\w*.\f + \fr 18:6 \ft Literally \fqa to uncover (their) nakedness\ft ; here and throughout this chapter\f* \w I|strong="H589"\w* \w am the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*.
\p \v 7 \w You must not|strong="H3808"\w* \w expose the nakedness|strong="H6172"\w* \w of your father|strong="H1"\w* \w by having sexual relations with|strong="H1540"\w* \w your mother|strong="H517"\w*. \w She|strong="H1931"\w* \w is your mother|strong="H517"\w*; \w you must not|strong="H3808"\w* \w have sexual relations with her|strong="H1540"\w*.
